---
source: crates/m2-server-core/tests/scenarios.rs
expression: h.log
---
-- a client of another version is refused, with the versions this server speaks
@1000 conn#1 accepted on auth from 10.0.0.1
   -> event: conn#1: accepted on auth
@1000 conn#1 sends Hello protocol=5 "openm2 test"
   -> event: conn#1: openm2 test speaks protocol 5
   -> event: conn#1: refused: another version of the protocol
   -> send conn#1 Refused reason=1 versions 4-4 "This server speaks another version of openm2."
   -> close conn#1
   -> event: conn#1: closed: another version of the protocol
-- anything before Hello closes the connection
@1000 conn#2 accepted on auth from 10.0.0.1
   -> event: conn#2: accepted on auth
@1000 conn#2 sends StartSignIn
   -> close conn#2
   -> event: conn#2: closed: a message before Hello
-- Hello is welcomed; a second one closes the connection
@1000 conn#3 accepted on game from 10.0.0.1
   -> event: conn#3: accepted on game
@1000 conn#3 sends Hello protocol=4 "openm2 test"
   -> event: conn#3: openm2 test speaks protocol 4
   -> send conn#3 Welcome protocol=4
@1000 conn#3 sends Hello protocol=4 "openm2 test"
   -> close conn#3
   -> event: conn#3: closed: a Hello after the Hello
-- a build with control characters is logged without them
@1000 conn#4 accepted on auth from 10.0.0.1
   -> event: conn#4: accepted on auth
@1000 conn#4 sends Hello protocol=4 "evil\nline"
   -> event: conn#4: evil?line speaks protocol 4
   -> send conn#4 Welcome protocol=4
-- no Hello in 10 s closes the connection
@1000 conn#5 accepted on game from 10.0.0.1
   -> event: conn#5: accepted on game
@11001 tick
   -> close conn#5
   -> event: conn#5: closed: no Hello in time
